    "text" : "• Submit the Fee Deferment Request form on the Student Portal with supporting documents (family income\n\nproof, medical/emergency documentation).\n\n• The Financial Aid Committee reviews applications within 7 working days and communicates the decision.\n\n• Approved deferments grant an extension of up to 30 days with no late fee penalty during the approved\n\nextension period.\n\n• A student may request deferment at most once per academic year.\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 7\n\n5. Refund Policy\n\nThe refund policy applies when a student voluntarily withdraws from the programme, is removed for\n\nnon-academic reasons, or when the institution fails to deliver services paid for. Refunds are processed as per\n\nthe schedule below, subject to administrative deductions.\n\nWhen Withdrawal Occurs\nRefund\n\n%\nItems Refunded Processing Time\n\nBefore commencement of\nclasses (pre-admission\nwithdrawal)\n\n100% of\nTuition\nFee\n\nTuition only; Registration fee\nnon-refundable\n\nWithin 30 working days\n\nWithin 15 days of class\ncommencement\n\n80% of\nSemester\nTuition\nFee\n\nTuition (proportionate); Exam fee\nretained\n\nWithin 30 working days\n\n16 to 30 days after\ncommencement\n\n50% of\nSemester\nTuition\nFee\n\nProportionate; all other fees\nretained\n\nWithin 45 working days\n\n31 to 60 days after\ncommencement\n\n25% of\nSemester\nTuition\nFee\n\nProportionate; all other fees\nretained\n\nWithin 45 working days\n\nAfter 60 days of\ncommencement\n\n0% refund No refund of any semester fees N/A\n\nCaution Deposit — at\ngraduation\n\n100%\n(less ded\nuctions)\n\nDeducted: property damage,\nlibrary dues, outstanding fees\n\nWithin 60 working days of\ngraduation\n\nDeath of a student (any time)\n\n100% of\nremaining\nsemester\ntuition\n\nFull semester tuition for\nunexpired period; to legal heir\n\nWithin 30 working days of\ndocumentation\n\n5.1 Refund Process\n\n• Submit a written Withdrawal / Refund Application to the Registrar's office with supporting documents.\n\n• Attach all original receipts of fee payments made.\n\n• Complete the institution's No-Dues clearance (library, lab, hostel, sports, TPC) before refund is\n\nprocessed.\n\n• Refunds are credited to the original payment source (bank account from which payment was made).\n\n• If payment was made by DD, the refund cheque is issued in the name of the payer.\n\n• Disputes regarding refund amounts must be escalated in writing to the Dean of Finance within 15 days of\n\nreceiving refund notification.",
