    "text" : "Rechecking Fee ■250 per subject Within 15 days of result declaration\n\nDuplicate Hall Ticket ■100\nOn request, at least 2 days before\nexam\n\nTranscript (Sealed Official) ■500 per set\nOn application; 7 working days\nprocessing time\n\nMigration Certificate ■500 On application; 15 working days\n\nProvisional Certificate (early graduation) ■300\nOn application after degree\nrequirements met\n\nDuplicate ID Card ■200 On application\n\nLate Registration Penalty ■500 flat\nIf registering after the official\nregistration window\n\nCertificate Attestation Fee ■100 per document\nFor institutional attestation of\ndocuments\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 5\n\n3. Fee Payment Schedule\n\nSemester Fee Due Date Items Payable\n\nOdd Semester\n(July–November)\n\nOn or before July 15 each\nyear\n\nTuition, Exam, Lab fees + all Annual fees (Library,\nTechnology, Sports, Activity, ID Card)\n\nEven Semester\n(January–May)\n\nOn or before January 15\neach year\n\nTuition, Exam, Lab fees for Even Semester only\n\nBacklog Exam\nRegistration\n\nAs per announcement\n(usually 4–6 weeks before\nsupplementary exams)\n\nBacklog exam fee per subject registered\n\nOne-Time fees at\nadmission\n\nWithin 7 days of admission\nconfirmation\n\nRegistration Fee + Caution Deposit\n\n3.1 Accepted Payment Modes\n\nPayment Mode Available For Receipt\n\nOnline — UPI (GPay,\nPhonePe, Paytm)\n\nAll fee types via Student Portal Instant digital receipt; downloadable PDF\n\nOnline — Net Banking / IMPS /\nNEFT\n\nAll fee types via Student Portal\nInstant digital receipt after bank\nconfirmation\n\nOnline — Credit / Debit Card\nAll fee types (processing fee\nmay apply)\n\nInstant digital receipt\n\nDemand Draft (DD)\nIn person at Accounts Office;\npayable to institution name\n\nPhysical receipt at counter\n\nScholarship / Fee Waiver\nCredit\n\nApplied directly against\noutstanding fee balance\n\nAdjusted in fee statement\n\n■ Note: Cash payments are accepted ONLY for amounts below ■2,000 and ONLY at the Accounts Office\n\ncounter. Always collect a signed receipt for cash payments.\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 6\n\n4. Late Fee Policy\n\nFees not paid by the due date attract a late fee surcharge. Students are encouraged to pay early; the\n\ninstitution sends reminders via email and SMS 2 weeks and 3 days before every due date.\n\nDays Beyond Due\nDate\n\nLate Fee\nSurcharge\n\nAdditional Academic Impact\n\n1 – 7 days late ■ 200 flat Friendly reminder; no academic restriction\n\n8 – 15 days late ■ 500 flat\nPortal access restricted; cannot view grades or download\ndocuments\n\n16 – 30 days late ■ 1,000 flat Classroom access may be restricted; HOD notified\n\n31 – 45 days late\n■ 1,500 flat + ■\n50/day from day 31\n\nAttendance marking suspended; parent notified by registered\npost\n\n46 – 60 days late\n■ 1,500 + ■ 50/day\naccrued\n\nExcluded from CIA assessments (unable to write mid-terms); at\nrisk of semester cancellation\n\nBeyond 60 days\nFull late fee\naccrued +\nescalation\n\nName removed from rolls; semester cancelled; re-admission\nrequired\n\n4.1 Fee Deferment Request\n\n• Students facing genuine financial hardship may apply for a fee deferment BEFORE the due date.\n\n• Applications submitted after the due date are NOT eligible for deferment (but may qualify for a payment\n\nplan).",
