    "text" : "Fee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 1\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy\nFee Breakdown · Payment Schedule · Late Fees · Refund & Withdrawal\n\nTransparent fee management framework for all enrolled students\n\nDocument Code: DOC-FEE-010\n\nVersion: v1.0 | March 2026\n\nAcademic Affairs & Administration\n\nPrepared By Academic\nAffairs Office\n\nStatus Active Review Cycle Annual\nClassification Internal\nUse Only\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 2\n\n1. Overview & Fee Philosophy\n\nThe institution is committed to transparency in financial matters. All fees are clearly communicated in the\n\nofficial Fee Notification issued at the start of each academic year. This document describes the components\n\nof fees, payment timelines, penalties for late payment, and the conditions under which fees may be refunded.\n\nFees are collected to support the operational, academic, and infrastructure needs of the institution. All fee\n\ncollections are routed through the official payment system; cash payments above ■2,000 are not accepted.\n\nStudents are entitled to a detailed receipt for every payment made.\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 3\n\n2. Fee Components — Comprehensive Breakdown\n\n2.1 Recurring Semester Fees\n\nFee Component Frequency Who Pays Description\n\nTuition Fee\nPer\nSemester\n\nAll students\nCore cost of academic instruction, faculty, and\nlearning resources\n\nExamination Fee\nPer\nSemester\n\nAll students\nRegistration for all CIA and ESE components;\nincludes result processing\n\nLaboratory / Consumables\nFee\n\nPer\nSemester\n\nStudents\nregistered in\nlab-intensive\nsubjects\n\nChemicals, materials, consumables, and\nequipment maintenance for labs\n\nPractical Examination Fee\nPer\nSemester (if\napplicable)\n\nStudents with\npractical ESE\n\nExternal examiner charges for practical\nend-semester exams\n\nStudent Welfare Fund\nPer\nSemester\n\nAll students\nAccident insurance, emergency medical fund,\nstudent welfare activities\n\n2.2 Annual Fees\n\nFee Component Frequency Description\n\nLibrary Fee\n\nAnnual\n(charged with\nOdd\nSemester)\n\nPhysical + digital library access; journal subscriptions; library\nmanagement\n\nTechnology & Platform Fee Annual\nLMS, campus Wi-Fi, student portal, email accounts, cloud\nstorage allocation\n\nSports & Physical Education\nFee\n\nAnnual\nSports facilities, equipment, coaching, inter-institutional\ncompetition registration\n\nStudent Activity & Cultural\nFee\n\nAnnual\nCultural events, annual day, student clubs, inter-college fest\nparticipation\n\nIdentity Card Fee Annual\nPrinting, encoding, and maintenance of smart campus ID\ncards\n\n2.3 One-Time Fees\n\nFee Structure & Refund Policy DOC-FEE-010  |  March 2026\n\nFor Internal Institutional Use Only — Do Not Distribute Page 4\n\nFee Component When Paid\nRefundable\n\n?\nDescription\n\nAdmission Registration\nFee\n\nAt time of\nadmission\n\nNo\nAdministrative cost of processing admission;\nnon-refundable under all circumstances\n\nCaution Deposit / Security\nDeposit\n\nAt time of\nadmission\n\nYes (at\ngraduation)\n\nRefundable deposit against loss/damage to\ninstitutional property\n\nAlumni Association Fee Final year No\nLifetime membership of the institution's\nalumni network\n\n2.4 Miscellaneous & On-Demand Fees\n\nFee Item Approx. Amount When Payable\n\nBacklog Exam Registration Fee ■300 per subject\nAt time of backlog registration each\nsemester\n\nRevaluation Fee ■600 per subject Within 20 days of result declaration",
